<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="Account and Data Deletion Policy for Highway Runner by Dreamup Studio">
  <title>Account &amp; Data Deletion Policy | Highway Runner</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --text: #222222;
      --muted: #667085;
      --border: #e5e7eb;
      --panel: #f8fafc;
      --link: #b91c1c;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: #ffffff;
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .container {
      width: min(920px, calc(100% - 32px));
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 48px 0 64px;
    }

    header {
      margin-bottom: 36px;
      padding-bottom: 24px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 20px;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
      line-height: 1.15;
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 42px 0 14px;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      line-height: 1.3;
    }

    p {
      margin: 10px 0 16px;
    }

    ul {
      margin: 8px 0 18px 24px;
      padding: 0;
    }

    li {
      margin: 5px 0;
    }

    .meta,
    .contact-box {
      background: var(--panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 18px 20px;
    }

    .meta {
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

    .meta p,
    .contact-box p {
      margin: 4px 0;
    }

    .contact-box {
      margin: 14px 0 20px;
    }

    a {
      color: var(--link);
      text-decoration: none;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    a:hover,
    a:focus {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .footer {
      margin-top: 48px;
      padding-top: 20px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .container {
        width: min(100% - 24px, 920px);
        padding-top: 28px;
      }

      h2 {
        margin-top: 34px;
      }

      body {
        font-size: 15.5px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="container">
    <header>
      <h1>Account &amp; Data Deletion Policy</h1>

      <div class="meta">
        <p><strong>Game:</strong> Highway Runner</p>
        <p><strong>Developer:</strong> Dreamup Studio</p>
        <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> 18 August 2026</p>
        <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> 18 August 2026</p>
      </div>

      <p>Dreamup Studio provides players of Highway Runner with a way to request deletion of their account and associated personal information.</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Requesting Account Deletion</h2>
      <p>Where an account deletion option is available inside Highway Runner, you may initiate deletion through that feature.</p>
      <p>You may also submit a deletion request by email.</p>
      <p>Send your request to:</p>

      <div class="contact-box">
        <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support.dreamup@gmail.com">support.dreamup@gmail.com</a></p>
        <p><strong>Subject:</strong> Highway Runner – Account Deletion Request</p>
      </div>

      <p>Please provide sufficient information to identify the Highway Runner account you want deleted, such as your registered email address or player/account identifier.</p>
      <p><strong>Never send your password.</strong></p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Verification</h2>
      <p>To protect players from unauthorized account deletion, Dreamup Studio may take reasonable steps to verify that the person requesting deletion is the account owner.</p>
      <p>Additional information may be requested where necessary to verify the request.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Information That May Be Deleted</h2>
      <p>Depending on the information associated with your account, deletion may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Highway Runner account information;</li>
        <li>Email address associated with the Highway Runner account;</li>
        <li>Player profile information;</li>
        <li>Stored game progress associated with the account;</li>
        <li>Account-linked scores;</li>
        <li>Leaderboard information associated with the account, where technically and legally appropriate; and</li>
        <li>Other personal information associated with the account that Dreamup Studio is not required or permitted to retain.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The exact data affected depends on the Highway Runner features and services used by the player.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Leaderboard Information</h2>
      <p>Deleting an account may result in the player's name and associated leaderboard information being deleted, anonymized or otherwise disassociated from the deleted account where appropriate.</p>
      <p>Technical limitations of third-party leaderboard systems may affect how historical leaderboard information is removed.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Information That May Be Retained</h2>
      <p>Certain limited information may be retained after an account deletion request where necessary or permitted for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Legal compliance;</li>
        <li>Security;</li>
        <li>Fraud and abuse prevention;</li>
        <li>Enforcement of our Terms of Service;</li>
        <li>Resolving disputes;</li>
        <li>Financial or transaction records where legally required; or</li>
        <li>Backup and disaster-recovery systems for a limited period.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Information retained for these purposes will not be used to continue normal operation of the deleted player account.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Processing Time</h2>
      <p>Dreamup Studio will process valid deletion requests within a reasonable period and within any timeframe required by applicable law.</p>
      <p>Additional time may be necessary where identity or account ownership needs to be verified or where technical limitations apply.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Consequences of Account Deletion</h2>
      <p>Account deletion may be permanent.</p>
      <p>Once deletion has been completed, you may lose access to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your Highway Runner account;</li>
        <li>Saved progress;</li>
        <li>High scores;</li>
        <li>Leaderboard records;</li>
        <li>Achievements;</li>
        <li>Account-linked settings; and</li>
        <li>Other information associated with the deleted account.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Deleted information may not be recoverable.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Guest Accounts</h2>
      <p>Guest accounts may work differently from registered accounts.</p>
      <p>Depending on how guest information is stored, deleting Highway Runner or clearing application data may remove locally stored guest information.</p>
      <p>Where guest information is stored by Dreamup Studio or a service provider and can be associated with a particular player, you may contact us for assistance with a deletion request.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Third-Party Accounts</h2>
      <p>Deleting a Highway Runner account does not necessarily delete your separate Google, Facebook or other third-party account.</p>
      <p>Similarly, deleting or disconnecting a third-party account does not necessarily constitute a request to delete information held by Highway Runner.</p>
      <p>You may need to manage information held independently by third-party providers through their own account and privacy controls.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Questions About Data Deletion</h2>
      <p>For questions concerning account or personal data deletion, contact:</p>

      <div class="contact-box">
        <p><strong>Dreamup Studio</strong></p>
        <p><strong>Game:</strong> Highway Runner</p>
        <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support.dreamup@gmail.com">support.dreamup@gmail.com</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="footer">
      <p>© 2026 Dreamup Studio. All rights reserved.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
